###

### ========================================================================
### COMMON API PATTERNS
### ========================================================================

### Error Response Format
# All endpoints return errors in this format:
# {
#   "error": "Human-readable error message"
# }

### Pagination Pattern
# Use query parameters for pagination:
# GET /api/processes?skip=0&take=50
# GET /api/deployments?processKey=my-process

### Filtering Patterns
# By state: GET /api/processes?state=Running
# By type: GET /api/incidents?type=FailedJob
# By status: GET /api/incidents?resolved=false

### Sorting Patterns
# Most endpoints return results in logical order:
# - Processes: by creation date (newest first)
# - Deployments: by version (highest first)
# - Incidents: by creation date (newest first)
# - Execution nodes: by sequence order

### ========================================================================
### API RESPONSE CODES
### ========================================================================

# 200 OK - Successful GET/PUT operations
# 201 Created - Resource created successfully
# 204 No Content - Operation successful, no content returned
# 400 Bad Request - Invalid request data
# 404 Not Found - Resource not found
# 500 Internal Server Error - Server error
# 501 Not Implemented - Feature not yet implemented

### ========================================================================
### BPMN ELEMENT TYPES
### ========================================================================

# Supported BPMN element types in execution flow:
# - StartEvent, EndEvent
# - UserTask, ServiceTask, ScriptTask
# - ExclusiveGateway, ParallelGateway, InclusiveGateway
# - IntermediateCatchEvent, IntermediateThrowEvent
# - BoundaryEvent (Error, Timer, Message)

### ========================================================================
### PROCESS STATES
### ========================================================================

# Process states in queries:
# - Created: Process instance created but not started
# - Running: Process is actively executing
# - Completed: Process finished successfully
# - Failed: Process ended with error

### ========================================================================
### INCIDENT TYPES
### ========================================================================

# Incident types:
# - FailedJob: Job execution failed
# - FailedExternalTask: External task failed
# - Condition: Condition evaluation failed

### ========================================================================
### AUTHENTICATION & SECURITY
### ========================================================================

# Note: Current API has no authentication
# For production use, consider:
# - JWT Bearer tokens
# - API key authentication
# - OAuth2 integration
# - Role-based access control

### ========================================================================
### MONITORING & LOGGING
### ========================================================================

# All endpoints include comprehensive logging:
# - Request/response logging
# - Error tracking
# - Performance metrics
# - Audit trails

### ========================================================================
### RATE LIMITING
### ========================================================================

# Consider implementing rate limiting for:
# - Process start operations
# - Bulk operations
# - Query operations

### ========================================================================
### WEBHOOKS & CALLBACKS
### ========================================================================

# Future enhancements may include:
# - Process completion webhooks
# - Incident alert webhooks
# - Task assignment notifications

### ========================================================================
### INTEGRATION EXAMPLES
### ========================================================================

### JavaScript Client Integration
###
// Deploy process
const deployResponse = await fetch('/api/deployments', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({
        processKey: 'order-process',
        bpmnXml: bpmnContent,
        label: 'Order Processing Workflow'
    })
});

// Start process instance
const startResponse = await fetch('/api/processes/start', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({
        processKey: 'order-process',
        businessKey: 'order-123',
        variables: { amount: 99.99, customer: 'john@example.com' }
    })
});
const processData = await startResponse.json();

// Monitor execution
const executionFlow = await fetch(`/api/process-execution/${processData.processId}/flow`);
const flowData = await executionFlow.json();

// Handle incidents
const incidents = await fetch(`/api/incidents/process/${processData.processId}`);
const incidentData = await incidents.json();

if (incidentData.length > 0) {
    // Resolve incidents
    for (const incident of incidentData) {
        await fetch(`/api/incidents/${incident.id}/resolve`, {
            method: 'POST',
            headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify({
                message: 'Issue resolved automatically'
            })
        });
    }
}
